A||||1||mattmullins||4spd trans grinds on gears
Z||000000||mattmullins||05-24-99||07:34 PM||||I recently purchased an 86 SE V-6 fiero.  It is a 4 speed manual transmission.  The guy that I bought it off of said that the linkage needed adjusting.  Well I think that I got burnt.  But anyway, when i purchased it it shifted through all of the gears except for 4th  and you had to stop to get it.  After adjusting it we could get all the gears but 3rd and 4th ground a little bit.  I need to know what my problem is do i need a new transmission??? will any 2.8 GM V-6 manual transmission bolt up directly to the fiero's mounts??  We have adjusted the linkage a million times,  but to no avail.
Z||000001||Hock||05-25-99||11:53 AM||||if you adjusted the shift linkage by the book than the only problem that can exist is the a bad clutch.  that is an expensive fix for a fiero.  it requires replacement of the disc, pressure plate, throw out bearing, adn most of the time the thrust bushing.  also included you WILL also have to either rebuild or replace the the clutch master and slave cylinder.  good luck!!!!
